>      No acceptably small step size could be found. Perhaps the posterior is not continuous?'
>
> Anything obvious I am doing wrong in the code below?

I think your problem is in step().  Some other
code improvements suggested inline.

>
> model <- "
>    data {
>      int n;
>      int J;
>      int K;
>      int Y[n, J];
>      real X[n, K];
>      matrix[J, J] ID;

We really need an identity matrix constant.
So this could be:

transformed data {
    matrix[J,J] ID;
    ID <- unit_matrix(J);

}

>      real df;
>    }
>    parameters {
>      vector[J] Z[n];
>      real B[J, K];
>      cov_matrix[J] S;
>    }
>    model {
>      matrix[n, J] Mu;
>      real p[n, J];
>      for (j in 1:J) {
>        B[j] ~ normal(0, 100);
>      }

This can be vectorized to B ~ normal(0,100);

You might want a slightly tighter prior on B.

>      for (i in 1:n) {
>        for (j in 1:J) {
>          Mu[i, j] <- dot_product(B[j], X[i]);
>        }
>      }
>      S ~ inv_wishart(df, ID);
>      for (i in 1:n) {
>        Z[i] ~ multi_normal(col(Mu', i), S);

Doing Mu[i]', equivalently row(Mu,i)',
is more efficient than col(Mu',i).  The issue is
that Mu' makes a copy of the whole matrix during
the transpose.

>      }
>      for (i in 1:n) {
>        for (j in 1:J) {
>          p[i, j] <- step(Z[i][j]);
>        }
>      }
>      for (i in 1:n) {
>        for (j in 1:J) {
>          Y[i, j] ~ bernoulli(p[i, j]);
>        }
>      }
>    }

Unless you need to see the p[i,j], I'd suggest removing
the first loop and replacing the inner part of the second
with bernoulli(step(Z[i,j]));

But now that I see what's up here, I think the step function
is probably your problem.  It returns either 0 or 1.

I think what you want to do is more like:

    Y[i,j] ~ bernoulli(inv_logit(Z[i,j]));

Or you can use Phi instead of inv_logit if you prefer
probit.

- Bob

I think the step=>bernoulli thing was just a way of implementing the
multivariate probit model. Using inv_logit() instead would result in a
sort of overdispersed probit model, which I don't think is what was
desired. I just sent an email summarizing our earlier discussion from
stan-dev about my issues with MV probits.

Matt

