Thanks, Matt!  This is totally going in the manual.

We need to upgrade some of the BUGS model translations
(like the circle and doughnut) which can be made much
neater using some of these tricks.

Ever since I started thinking about unit hyperspheres,
I keep thinking we should be able to neatly parameterize
them via constraints.  For instance, we can constrain x
directly to be scaled to the unit circle:

   parameters {
       real<lower=-1,upper=1> x;

The problem is that then y = +/- sqrt(1 - x^2).
That is, we only need a sign out of y once we have x.

In 3 dimensions, it's the same problem:

       real<lower=-1,lower=1> x;
       real<lower=-sqrt(1 - x * x),upper=sqrt(1 - x * x)> y;
       ?? z

The atan2 deals with both the scale and the sign (and
answers the question of "who uses atan2?" I had when
coding the auto-dif lib).  And I'm pretty sure it scales
up neatly to hyperspheres.

Matt's reparameterization of the Cauchy is also going in
the manual (as well as into the appendix of the
next edition of BDA in Andrew's discussion of
HMC in R).

- Bob

